> >would be brivla, PA, KOhA, and I JA (or the
> corresponding Polish
> >notation).  

Also:

NOI-KUhO, if you want to include restricted quantification.

ZOhU, SE or FA, otherwise you can only quantify in the 
default order imposed by the brivla arguments. SE and FA
are probably not enough for all cases though, so make 
it ZOhU.

XI so you don't run out of variables.

TUhE-TUhU, otherwise you can't get all groupings of the 
connectives. (If you use GA GI instead if I JA you don't 
need these.)

NA and probably KU as well, for negations.

